    <briefdescription>
<para>A proxy object for concisely formatting large contiguous numeric ranges. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Instead of iterating and printing every element of a massive sequence, this formatter intelligently truncates the output using an ellipsis (e.g., <computeroutput>{0, ..., 99}</computeroutput>).</para>
<sect3 id="structgl_1_1io_1_1implicit__range__formatter_1example-usage-18">
<title>Example Usage</title>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">std::cout<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/>gl::io::implicit_range_formatter&lt;int&gt;{0,<sp/>100}<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;\n&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::cout<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/>gl::io::implicit_range_formatter&lt;int&gt;{5,<sp/>8}<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="charliteral">&apos;\n&apos;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><bold>Output:</bold> <programlisting filename=".text"><codeline><highlight class="normal">{0,<sp/>...,<sp/>99}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{5,<sp/>...,<sp/>7}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect3>
